+**Potential reviewer concerns:** They will likely flag any lack of real data validation, unclear methodology (especially the reconstruction approach for forecasting), and any "machine learning hype". We must be careful not to claim “novelty” beyond combining known modules. The novelty is in rigorous evaluation and insight (including negative results). They will also look for reproducibility: commit hashes (4e9e4be… as given), data citations (gridMET, SNODAS, CAMELS), and complete author disclosure (the repository indicates authorship by Adi Shrestha; any changes must be credited). 
